complete the original task, then retain a photograph or short parent observation as evidence.","outcome_codes":["HS2-GEO-01"],"parent_notes":"Parent: Marking guidance for the independent task: Choose one coastal and one inland town. Use a published climate source to write two differences and give at least two causes for each, using words such as distance from the equator, coast and height. Accept equivalent original responses that show the same skill.\n\nParent: Written model 1: Original response on new material: Canberra is higher above sea level and further from the sea''s mild influence, so winter nights are colder and frosts are more common. Reasoning: I used climate by attending to coast and explain why it matters rather than copying the worked model.\n\nParent: Written model 2: Common error: Saying \"they are different because they are different places\" gives no cause that can be checked against a map or data. Correction: Canberra is higher above sea level and further from the sea''s mild influence, so winter nights are colder and frosts are more common. Why: the correction restores accurate use of climate.\n\nParent: Likely misconception: Saying \"they are different because they are different places\" gives no cause that can be checked against a map or data. Keep sample answers out of the child role.\n\nParent: Short-answer focus 1: Produce a fresh example demonstrating climate on new material (not the worked model). Explain the particular words, sources or choices that make it work.\n\nParent: Short-answer focus 2: Name one likely error with climate, correct it, and explain why the correction helps a reader or audience.\n\nParent: Marking notes: Require independently produced work with a specific supporting detail. / Require misconception + correction + purpose-linked reason..","pass":1,"pass_mark":0.9,"planner_fields":null,"planner_intro":null,"planner_title":null,"printable_resource":null,"quiz":[{"correct_index":1,"explanation":"Canberra is higher above 